Training data
- Mozilla Common Voice 27.0, Turkish (CC0 1.0). The released voice is an anonymous Common Voice contributor.
- ISSAI Turkish Speech Corpus (MIT), Institute of Smart Systems and Artificial Intelligence, Nazarbayev University.
  Mussakhojayeva et al., "Multilingual Speech Recognition for Turkic Languages", Information 14(2):74, 2023.
- MediaSpeech, Turkish (CC BY 4.0). Kolobov et al., "MediaSpeech: Multilanguage ASR Benchmark and Dataset", 2021.
- Google FLEURS, Turkish (CC BY 4.0). Conneau et al., "FLEURS: Few-shot Learning Evaluation of Universal
  Representations of Speech", 2022.

Models used during training only (not redistributed)
- ACE-Step 1.5 VAE (MIT): audio → 64-dim latents for training targets.
- mpoyraz/wav2vec2-xls-r-300m-cv7-turkish (CC BY 4.0): forced alignment of letter durations.

Software used at run time
- normalizer-tr (Apache-2.0), Erdem Tuna: Turkish text normalization (Python package and Rust crate).
- ONNX Runtime and ONNX Runtime Web (MIT), Microsoft.
- lamejs (@breezystack/lamejs, LGPL-3.0), a JavaScript port of LAME: MP3 export on the demo page, loaded unmodified
  as a separate file only when MP3 is chosen.
- Courier Prime and Archivo typefaces (SIL Open Font License 1.1) on the demo page.

Evaluation
- Freya-TR-Eval (freyavoice/freya-tr-eval, CC BY 4.0): evaluation sentences, never used for training.
- Whisper-large-v3 (Apache-2.0), OpenAI; UTMOS22 (MIT), SaruLab.

Architecture
- The pipeline follows the public description of EMA Lightning (canberkkkkkk/ema-lightning, Apache-2.0); this is an
  independent implementation trained from scratch. No EMA Lightning weights are included.
